is all three anre npm packages?

Yes — all three are npm packages, published on npmjs.com (npm's public registry).

npm/npx is to Node.js what yum is to RHEL/CentOS — a package manager that fetches and installs software from a central registry.

+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| RHEL world                             | Node.js world                                                 |
+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| yum install nginx                      | npm install -g package-name                                  |
+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Registry: RHEL/EPEL repos              | Registry: npmjs.com (npm's public registry)                  |
+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Installs permanently                   | npm install -g = permanent; npx = temporary, one-time run    |
+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| rpm -qa (list installed)               | npm list -g (list installed)                                 |
+----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+

• When Claude Desktop ran npx -y package-name, it fetched that package from
  npmjs.com's servers, downloaded it temporarily, and executed it
  — similar to yum install pulling from a repo, except npx doesn't leave it
  permanently installed (each restart re-fetches, though npm caches it
  locally so it's fast after the first time).

One more parallel worth noting, given your Docker background:

• npx behaves a bit like docker run
  (ephemeral, runs and can be discarded)

• npm install -g behaves more like yum install
  (persists on the system)
