Simplest option (npx-based, similar to what we did for Kubernetes/GitHub):

There's an actively maintained one, kud/mcp-jenkins, that covers roughly 95%
of the Jenkins API — jobs, builds, nodes, views, queue, plugins, and system
operations, with zero-install usage via npx.

Setup steps:

1. Generate a Jenkins API token:

   • Log into Jenkins -> click your username (top right) -> Configure

   • Under API Token -> Add new Token -> Generate

   • Copy it immediately

Edit the same config file (Edit Config in Settings → Developer):

"mcpServers": {
  "kubernetes": {
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "kubernetes-mcp-server@latest"],
    "env": {
      "KUBECONFIG": "C:\\Users\\kamalesh parthiban\\.kube\\config"
    }
  },
  "github": {
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
    "env": {
      "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "your_github_token_here"
    }
  },
  "jenkins": {
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "@kud/mcp-jenkins@latest"],
    "env": {
      "JENKINS_URL": "http://107.20.118.73:8080",
      "JENKINS_USER": "kamalesh",
      "JENKINS_API_TOKEN": "your_jenkins_token_here"
    }
  }
}

